WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.499
- [Narrator] Russian flags,
photos of the Russian president

00:00:04.499 --> 00:00:06.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.811
and children dancing to a
patriotic Russian pop song.

00:00:10.811 --> 00:00:12.390
(nationalistic music)

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.430
These images from Ukrainian schools

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.610
and nurseries show the Kremlin's
efforts to give children

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.940
in the occupied territories
a Russian identity.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.530
- The change at schools are one

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.740
of the most obvious, simplest
forms of Russification.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.840
- [Narrator] The Wall Street
Journal examined videos

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.480
and photos shared by Russian authorities

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.280
to understand how Moscow is trying

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.343
to influence children
in the occupied regions.

00:00:36.815 --> 00:00:40.732
(Vladimir speaking in Russian)

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.860
- [Narrator] Russia has been pushing

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.730
to incorporate four partially
occupied Ukrainian regions

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.820
into its legal, social
and economic systems

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.602
ever since it claimed
to annex them in 2022.

00:00:56.602 --> 00:01:00.840
(people chanting in Russian)

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.780
Education has been key to these efforts.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.190
Official posts show children

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.020
in the occupied regions learning

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.800
about the life of the composer
of Russia's national anthem,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.020
celebrating Russian Science Day

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.270
and drawing the annexed Crimean peninsula

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.670
in the colors of the Russian flag.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.840
- They're pushing a very
patriotic, pro-Russian curriculum.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.790
- The Wall Street
Journal's Ian Lovett spoke

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.180
with families whose children
attended Russian-run schools

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.270
in areas retaken by Ukrainian forces,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.670
as well as teachers who work there.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.430
They told him that schools
under Russia's administration

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:39.549
largely left Ukraine and its
history out of the curriculum.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:42.210
(nationalistic music)

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.950
- In the morning, at some schools,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.470
the kids have to sing the national anthem.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.980
There's now classes conducted
exclusively in Russian.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.950
There is still, in some schools,
Ukrainian language class

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.550
but it's now taught as a foreign language.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.830
- [Narrator] The Journal found
this document in a school

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.300
in the Kharkiv region,

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.480
outlining the goals of
secondary education.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.390
One of them is to form
a Russian civic identity

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.100
among the students.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.430
Moscow's efforts to
Russify Ukrainian children,

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.350
were also documented in a report

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.870
by the Yale School of Public Health.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.260
It accused the Kremlin of
relocating Ukrainian children

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.310
to Russia and reeducating
them to become pro-Russian.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.473
Following this report,

00:02:24.473 --> 00:02:27.720
the State Department said
there was mounting evidence

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.700
of the Kremlin's aims to deny

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.870
and suppress Ukrainian
identity, history, and culture.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.660
- The schools in occupied
territory also have the goal

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.950
of turning them into Russian children.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.470
I think they're hoping
that in a generation,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.800
they won't have as many
Ukrainians to fight against.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.000
- [Narrator] Moscow denied having

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.790
forcefully relocated Ukrainian children,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.740
despite multiple official images

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.503
showing Ukrainian orphans
arriving in Russia.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.370
The Kremlin also denied
having special programs aimed

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.980
at the Russification of Ukrainian children

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.650
and said it creates
opportunities for all children

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.263
in Russia to study their native languages.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.980
Ukrainian children are not only targets

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.670
of Russian propaganda, they
also became integral to it

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.220
as official photos and videos show.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.190
- Schools themselves and
the kids who attend them

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:20.070
have been turned into parts
of Russian propaganda,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.100
which I think is mostly
targeting Russian citizens

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.420
inside of Russia, with the goal

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.700
of showing them that
these Ukrainian regions

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.700
are eagerly accepting our
liberation is what they call it.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.700
- [Narrator] Here, school
children form the shape of a star

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.700
and hold Russian flags to
commemorate the Defender

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.290
of the Fatherland Day,

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.740
a holiday which celebrates
Russia's armed forces.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.390
And these are letters children wrote

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.840
to Russian soldiers on
the front line in Ukraine.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.330
One letter shows a
Russian flag and a tank,

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.723
and wishes soldiers health,
strength, and victories.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.100
Schools across Russia
have placed more emphasis

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.913
on patriotic education since
the invasion of Ukraine began.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.240
But the consequences for children

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.230
in occupied Ukrainian regions
could be far reaching.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.260
- Even if the occupation
doesn't last for forever

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.750
in some of these areas,
if they get six months

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.490
or a year or two years with these kids,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.590
that's probably gonna have
a very profound impact

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.839
on the way those kids think
about Ukraine and Russia.

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:24.506
(pensive music)

